# TX-F1 (W-TX's fault, writer 10). L §5.19 Booking an observation: "Each end of an observed leg is booked at its place
# from the observation of the version that covers that place on that day"; L §6.1: "Movements stated same, observed rows
# among them, are one movement ... booked once at each place. A place one of them books (an observed row books where its
# statement covers, §5.19) takes that one's legs"; L §5.19 Coverage: the planned movements that touch a covered place on
# a covered day before K are the modelled past, "never booked", and "its observations stand in for it where they are
# booked".
# The contrast with fulfils: gift in place of the same line: the row fulfils the instance and stands in for it: 5 000.00 DUK, as snap14.
=== m.tally
model one
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2024-12-31

source s "made up"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place acc: accounts DUK lives 2024-01-01..

place other: outside lives 2024-01-01..

input stmt: observed

input g_day: date

input g_amt: money DUK

move gift: transfers
  on g_day
  leg cash from other to acc amount g_amt

ask q: flows(acc, 2024)

version v
  cite s
  governs 2024-05
  known 2024-05-02
  covers acc
  stmt[r1] = (on: 2024-05-02, kind: transfers, leg cash from other to acc amount 5000.00 DUK, fulfils: gift) "r1"

version plan
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2024-01-01
  g_day = 2024-05-02 "plan"
  g_amt = 5000.00 "plan"
=== expect
q: 5 000.00 DUK
  cut 2026-10-25
